(* All SenseTalk date/time values fundamentally represent a point on the time line.

A date/time value also has a format, which controls how it is displayed. Changing the format doesn't change its value on the time line.
*)

put the time into myTime
put myTime
put myTime's format
put -

convert myTime to short date and long time
put myTime
put myTime's format
put -

set myTime's format to "[hr24] o'clock on day [day] of [monthName]"
put myTime
put -

convert myTime to abbr international time
put myTime
put myTime's format
put =

put myTime * 1 // a little hack to see the internal timeline value
put =

